{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CbrfaPWmCaj4rZJHM12rzS","type":"tool_result","content":"# Day 7 — Node by Node (script-analysis, node operation graphs)\n\nConcept: one evidence.zip with 61 members (PowerShell samples, JScript/Batch/VBScript/Python/Bash/Node operation\ngraphs); each graph decodes to a plan (steps/adapter/campaign/indicator) and is sorted into a role.\n\nVARIANT AXIS: none in the bytes. TT attempt 26b7da83 failed because its download was the GM body `{\"error\":\"rate_limited\"}` (24 B saved as evidence.zip, sha != contract sha256), so every field came out None/default. The harvested variants 49b73141 + 7d6f8d53 were already answered 469/469 by the current solver (spot-checked against the raw bytes; their expected.json is solver-derived, not GM-verified). Parse rule: if every artifact is a small `{\"error\": ...}` JSON, exit non-zero (solve.py now does) instead of guessing roles. The bytes-less case was removed from cases/ (still kept under time_trial/attempts/26b7da83).\n\nVARIANT AXIS: none (Day 8 TT). The start returned 503 `training_rotation_invalid` with no attempt and no artifact, so there were no variant bytes. The solver answers the TT contract's 615 ids 615/615 on the single's bytes. Rule: a start error is an orchestrator retry, not a solver change.\n\nVARIANT AXIS: none in the bytes (D8 Mastery 7432c509). Same 5-set bundle shape (outer zip holding evidence-01..05.zip) as the GM-verified auto-mastery cases; the solver answered 3075/3075 but the attempt EXPIRED (submit RemoteDisconnected after 5.42 s solve on Homebase). expected.json = solver output, spot-checked against the raw bytes (PS base64 record, VBS Codec_ field, While/if-errorlevel control). Speed fix: sets solve in forked processes (group_by_set + ProcessPoolExecutor, sequential fallback); the nested-zip index no longer decrypts every script leaf just to sniff for PK (375 PBKDF2s -> only the members asked, per set, in parallel); powerplay.xor is one big-int XOR.\n\nVARIANT AXIS: none in the bytes (D8 Mastery 7432c509, re-flagged on D23). It is permanently UNVERIFIABLE: the D8 attempt EXPIRED (no GM grade), so expected.json stays {}. The D23 solver's 3075 answers equal the D8 solver's submission (mastery/attempts/7432c509/last_timed.json) 3075/3075, and that solver's other D8 Mastery runs were GM-verified. The real failure was SPEED: ~1100 serial AES PBKDF2s on the D23 Mastery bundle. Rule: the WinZip-AES salt sits right after each local header, so derive every member key up front in a thread pool (OpenSSL PBKDF2 releases the GIL) and look it up in the pyzipper PBKDF2 patch (\n====\n# binary-swift-justice solver notes\n\nVARIANT AXIS: Mastery set count (2 on auto-mastery-d1a6613c, up to 5 x 31 MB on D8) -- main() now groups (answer_id, question) pairs with lib.common.group_by_set and solves each set in a fork ProcessPoolExecutor (sequential fallback on pool error, HCTF_SOLVER_PARALLEL=0 disables); each set's delivery is still paired by contract sha256 via container_by_sha. Output identical to the sequential loop on all 9 cases.\n\nVARIANT AXIS: speed only (no answer change) -- the evidence.zip is all WinZip AE-2 (method 99, AES-256, deflate) and its 67 MB d08 Swift ELF was inflated serially through pyzipper (pure-Python HMAC-SHA1 + AES); unzip() now reads AES members directly (PBKDF2 + AES-CTR LE counter, pw-verifier check, no HMAC) in a thread pool, largest first, decrypt||inflate||sha256 pipelined for members > 8 MB, and returns Futures that group_members() resolves only for the group asked (falls back to the pyzipper reader on any miss). single 1.2 s -> 0.8 s local.\n\nVARIANT AXIS: speed only (no answer change; the 9.74 s was the harness's contention-measured Mastery estimate, real single = 0.5-0.6 s, 5-set Mastery 1.7-1.9 s pinned to 2 CPUs) -- per-set CPU trimmed: AE-2 members (CRC 0) skip the 67 MB crc32 pass, multi-set runs inflate the big member in one shot instead of the 3-thread pipeline (+20% CPU, ~0 wall), and the lazy deps (capstone/pefile/Cryptodome/lib.common) import once in the parent before forking. Floor: stock zlib inflate of the 67 MB d08 13:import argparse, importlib.util, json, os, re, subprocess, sys, tempfile\n19:from lib import codec  # noqa: E402\n20:from lib.common import ZIP_PASSWORDS, container_by_sha, delivery_missing, find_artifact, group_by_set, iter_files, load_contract, normalize, read_member as _lib_read_member  # noqa: E402\n21:from lib.common import _zip_open, _zip_read  # noqa: E402","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fda61a87-a4dc-42f1-b63a-c9c98cd4c46b","uuid":"f0af52c2-af98-4391-b3f2-0bbbbdce9912","timestamp":"2026-10-26T13:10:33.729Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# Day 7 — Node by Node (script-analysis, node operation graphs)\n\nConcept: one evidence.zip with 61 members (PowerShell samples, JScript/Batch/VBScript/Python/Bash/Node operation\ngraphs); each graph decodes to a plan (steps/adapter/campaign/indicator) and is sorted into a role.\n\nVARIANT AXIS: none in the bytes. TT attempt 26b7da83 failed because its download was the GM body `{\"error\":\"rate_limited\"}` (24 B saved as evidence.zip, sha != contract sha256), so every field came out None/default. The harvested variants 49b73141 + 7d6f8d53 were already answered 469/469 by the current solver (spot-checked against the raw bytes; their expected.json is solver-derived, not GM-verified). Parse rule: if every artifact is a small `{\"error\": ...}` JSON, exit non-zero (solve.py now does) instead of guessing roles. The bytes-less case was removed from cases/ (still kept under time_trial/attempts/26b7da83).\n\nVARIANT AXIS: none (Day 8 TT). The start returned 503 `training_rotation_invalid` with no attempt and no artifact, so there were no variant bytes. The solver answers the TT contract's 615 ids 615/615 on the single's bytes. Rule: a start error is an orchestrator retry, not a solver change.\n\nVARIANT AXIS: none in the bytes (D8 Mastery 7432c